        {"source": "spec", "quote": "- `J11` (Barrel_Jack) → `+12V` net."}
      ],
      "impact": "If J11 is shorted or loaded by an external connection, GPIO1 can be pulled low or driven into an unintended external circuit, potentially disabling the heater control or stressing the ESP32 GPIO. This creates an external control path not present in the intended design.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most connectivity matches the specification, but J11 is an extra screw terminal tied to the GPIO1 heater-control net and GND, which is not part of the intended design and creates an unintended external short/load path."
}

